url: "https://below-the-frost-line.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the founding and growth of Sarasota, Florida,
  from the Edinburgh prospectus of 1884 that offered land on Sarasota Bay
  "below the frost line" to the town's own history of 1946. Six modules with
  108 passages, each read against the page image of a public-domain printing:
  the prospectus, decisions of Florida's Supreme Court on the vigilance
  murders of 1884, newspapers from Pensacola, Atlanta, Chicago, Bradentown and
  Sarasota, promotional booklets, the census, the Weather Bureau, a federal
  hearing, a Civilian Conservation Corps camp paper, the NAACP's list of
  lynchings, and Karl H. Grismer's Story of Sarasota (1946, not renewed). It
  asks who was promised what, who came and who left, and who belonged to the
  town and who was kept at its edge. With 51 public-domain plates, 6 graphics,
  14 comparisons, a timeline of 53 stations, and a list of what is not
  carried and why. Companion game: A City of Glorified Opportunity (free).
